{"plan":"# LifeOS Permissions Matrix (+ Network VPN Control)\n\nSource of truth for features: [`.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md`](.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md). Stack remains **native Kotlin + Compose**. This plan does not re-scope the 3-hour build; it freezes **what each feature is allowed to touch on Android**, including the new network-restriction pillar.\n\n## Design decisions (locked)\n\n- **App UI blocking** stays on `UsageStatsManager` + `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` (no AccessibilityService).\n- **Network restriction** uses a local **`VpnService`** (same pattern as Blokada / AppBlock network modes): LifeOS becomes the device VPN endpoint and decides which apps/domains may leave the device. No root. No `WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS`.\n- Two complementary enforcement layers:\n  - **UI layer**: stop opening Instagram (overlay).\n  - **Network layer**: if they somehow stay in a browser/app, starve blacklisted destinations / non-whitelisted apps of connectivity.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Chat[Chat ActionExecutor] --> FocusRules[FocusRules]\n  FocusRules --> UIBlock[FocusService overlay]\n  FocusRules --> NetBlock[LifeOsVpnService]\n  UIBlock --> UsageStats[UsageStatsManager]\n  UIBlock --> Overlay[SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW]\n  NetBlock --> VpnConsent[VpnService.prepare]\n  NetBlock --> AppFilter[addAllowed or addDisallowedApplication]\n  NetBlock --> DnsFilter[Local DNS blacklist whitelist]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Feature → permission matrix (hackathon in-scope)\n\n| Feature | What it needs from the OS | Permissions / APIs | Grant path | Play / policy note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Chat + Gemini | Outbound HTTPS | `INTERNET` | Install-time | None |\n| Persist goals/tasks/XP/memory | Local storage | None beyond normal app storage | N/A | None |\n| Dashboard / risk % / streak | Read own DataStore | None | N/A | None |\n| Personality + TTS wake line | `TextToSpeech` | None | N/A | None |\n| Notifications (focus ongoing, alarm fallback, VPN status) | Post notifications | `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` | Runtime dialog (API 33+) | None |\n| Exact alarms / demo wake-up | `AlarmManager.setAlarmClock` | `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM` | Settings: `ACTION_REQUEST_SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM`; gate with `canScheduleExactAlarms()` | Do **not** use `USE_EXACT_ALARM` (clock-app only) |\n| Full-screen alarm Activity | Launch over lock screen | `USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT` | Install-time; on API 34+ may need Settings if not auto-granted — fallback to high-priority notification via `canUseFullScreenIntent()` | Prefer alarm-style FSI use |\n| Survive reboot (restore alarms + focus/VPN intent) | Boot broadcast | `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED` | Install-time | None |\n| Keep CPU awake briefly while scheduling / overlay | Partial wake | `WAKE_LOCK` | Install-time | None |\n| Alarm / block haptic | Vibrator | `VIBRATE` | Install-time | None |\n| Detect foreground app (Instagram/Chrome) | Usage access | `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS` | Settings: `ACTION_USAGE_ACCESS_SETTINGS`; verify via `AppOpsManager` | Low scrutiny vs Accessibility |\n| Focus block overlay | Draw over other apps | `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | Settings: `ACTION_MANAGE_OVERLAY_PERMISSION`; verify `Settings.canDrawOverlays()` | Also helps background activity launch |\n| Focus session process | Long-running monitor | `FOREGROUND_SERVICE`, `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE` + manifest `specialUse` property | Install-time; ongoing notification required | Declare special-use justification in Play form at release |\n| App picker for blocklist | Resolve launcher apps | Manifest `<queries>` for `MAIN`/`LAUNCHER` | N/A | Prefer this over `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES` |\n| **Network blacklist / whitelist** | Local VPN routing | `BIND_VPN_SERVICE` on service; `INTERNET`; FGS types below; user VPN consent | System VPN consent via `VpnService.prepare()`; optional Always-on VPN is user Settings | Play VPN declaration at release; disclose that traffic is filtered on-device |\n\n### Network restriction — concrete behavior\n\nImplement `LifeOsVpnService : VpnService` with:\n\n1. **App-level routing** (fast path, no packet parsing): `VpnService.Builder.addDisallowedApplication(pkg)` for blacklist *or* `addAllowedApplication(pkg)` for whitelist-only focus sessions. Whitelist mode always includes LifeOS itself plus critical system packages so the session cannot brick dialer/SMS unintentionally — keep an internal `SYSTEM_CRITICAL_ALLOW` set.\n2. **Domain-level filter** (for browser / YouTube / doomscroll sites): establish the TUN, run a local DNS stub on the VPN interface, answer NXDOMAIN / sinkhole for blacklist hostnames; in whitelist-network mode only resolve allowlisted hosts. Packet forwarding for allowed flows stays on-device (no remote VPN server).\n3. **LLM actions** extended: `network_block_apps`, `network_allow_apps`, `network_block_domains`, `network_allow_domains`, `network_mode` (`off` | `blacklist` | `whitelist`).\n4. **Demo pairing**: UI-block Instagram package **and** VPN-disallow its network (and optionally blacklist `instagram.com` / `youtube.com` for Chrome).\n\nVPN-related manifest extras:\n\n- Service: `android.permission.BIND_VPN_SERVICE`, intent filter `android.net.VpnService`.\n- FGS: reuse `FOREGROUND_SERVICE` + `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE` (same subtype property as FocusService), **or** a dedicated VPN FGS with the same type if split into two services. Both Focus and VPN need visible ongoing notifications while active.\n- Do not request `CONTROL_VPN` (system/signature only). Do not request location for “network control.”\n\n---\n\n## Onboarding grants (ordered)\n\nSingle permission screen, four special-access rows plus one runtime prompt:\n\n1. Notifications → `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`\n2. Exact alarms → `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM`\n3. Usage access → `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS`\n4. Display over other apps → `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW`\n5. **Network control (VPN)** → `VpnService.prepare()` activity result (system dialog: “LifeOS wants to set up a VPN connection”). Copy must say filtering is on-device for focus, not a privacy-invasive remote VPN.\n\nVerify before Focus / Network toggles enable: `canScheduleExactAlarms()`, usage AppOps, `canDrawOverlays()`, and `VpnService.prepare() == null` (already consented).\n\n---\n\n## Manifest declare list (canonical)\n\n**Normal / install-time**\n\n- `INTERNET`\n- `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`\n- `VIBRATE`\n- `WAKE_LOCK`\n- `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED`\n- `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM`\n- `USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT`\n- `FOREGROUND_SERVICE`\n- `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE`\n\n**Special access (declared; granted in Settings / system UI)**\n\n- `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS`\n- `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW`\n\n**Service-locked**\n\n- `BIND_VPN_SERVICE` (on `LifeOsVpnService` only)\n\n**Not a permission**\n\n- `<queries>` launcher intent (app picker)\n- TTS (no permission)\n- DataStore / serialization (no permission)\n\n---\n\n## Explicitly out of the declare list (and why)\n\n| Tempting API | Why avoided for LifeOS |\n| --- | --- |\n| `AccessibilityService` | Play declaration + disclosure; Android 15/17 Advanced Protection revokes non-tool access |\n| `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES` | Declaration form; `<queries>` is enough |\n| `USE_EXACT_ALARM` | Reserved for clock/calendar/alarm core apps |\n| `READ_SMS` / `READ_CALL_LOG` | Default-handler only — unobtainable |\n| `REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS` | Declaration friction; use OEM guides later |\n| Background location | Irrelevant to focus/VPN; high scrutiny |\n| Device Admin / MDM | Overkill; enterprise path only |\n| Root / `iptables` | Not shippable on stock devices |\n\n---\n\n## Vision-doc features (listed in existing plan audit) → permissions if ever built later\n\nThese are **not** hackathon scope, but mapped so the matrix is complete against the existing plan’s audit tables:\n\n| Vision item | Permission / mechanism |\n| --- | --- |\n| Calendar deadline sync | `READ_CALENDAR`, `WRITE_CALENDAR` |\n| Notification scraping (Gmail/Classroom) | `NotificationListenerService` + user enable in Notification access Settings |\n| Health (steps/sleep/HR) | Health Connect permissions + `ACTIVITY_RECOGNITION` |\n| Voice input to chat | `RECORD_AUDIO` |\n| Email via Gmail API | OAuth `gmail.readonly` — CASA for production, not a manifest permission |\n| Moodle/Piazza | No phone permission — account/API integration |\n\n---\n\n## Hard walls (unchanged, still true with VPN)\n\n- VPN **cannot** silently start: every session needs prior `prepare()` consent (or Always-on VPN toggled by the user in system Settings).\n- VPN **does not replace** UI blocking: a disallowed app can still open offline UI; overlay remains required for the “slams in front” demo.\n- Per-app `addAllowedApplication` / `addDisallowedApplication` fail if the package is not installed — handle gracefully.\n- Some OEMs kill VPN + FGS aggressively; no permission fixes that.\n- iOS network control is a different entitlement world; Android-only remains correct.\n\n---\n\n## Deliverable after approval\n\nUpdate [`.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md`](.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md) (or a sibling permissions plan file in `.cursor/plans/`) with this matrix, extend ActionExecutor action types for network rules, and add `LifeOsVpnService` + a fourth onboarding grant to the architecture diagram — **documentation/plan only unless you later ask to implement**.\n","todos":[{"id":"update-plan-doc","content":"Write permissions matrix + VPN pillar into .cursor/plans (extend hackathon plan or add sibling permissions plan)","status":"TODO_STATUS_PENDING","createdAt":"1788072096118","updatedAt":"1788072096118","dependencies":[]},{"id":"extend-actions","content":"Document new LLM/ActionExecutor network_* action types and FocusRules fields for app/domain black/whitelist","status":"TODO_STATUS_PENDING","createdAt":"1788072096118","updatedAt":"1788072096118","dependencies":[]},{"id":"onboarding-vpn","content":"Document 5-step onboarding grant order including VpnService.prepare and verification checks","status":"TODO_STATUS_PENDING","createdAt":"1788072096118","updatedAt":"1788072096118","dependencies":[]},{"id":"manifest-canonical","content":"Document canonical manifest permission/service/queries list including BIND_VPN_SERVICE and FGS specialUse","status":"TODO_STATUS_PENDING","createdAt":"1788072096118","updatedAt":"1788072096118","dependencies":[]}],"overview":"Complete Android permissions and capability matrix for every feature in the existing LifeOS hackathon plan, plus a VpnService-based network blacklist/whitelist layer that complements app-overlay focus enforcement.","name":"LifeOS Permissions Matrix","isProject":false,"phases":[]}
````

