{"path":"/opt/cursor/artifacts/plans/lifeos_permissions_matrix_36131bb8.plan.md","streamContent":"---\nname: LifeOS Permissions Matrix\noverview: \"Complete Android permissions matrix (including VpnService network blacklist/whitelist) plus a Cloud Agent environment that ships the Android SDK, adb platform-tools, and the full Kotlin/Gradle development toolchain.\"\ntodos:\n  - id: env-android-sdk\n    content: \"Configure Cloud Agent environment with JDK, Android cmdline-tools, platform-tools (adb), build-tools, and Android platform SDK; set ANDROID_HOME and PATH\"\n    status: pending\n  - id: env-validate-adb\n    content: \"Validate adb/sdkmanager/javac on the VM, snapshot, draft-build, and propose environment.json for Save\"\n    status: pending\n  - id: update-plan-doc\n    content: Write permissions matrix + VPN pillar into .cursor/plans (extend hackathon plan or add sibling permissions plan)\n    status: pending\n  - id: extend-actions\n    content: Document new LLM/ActionExecutor network_* action types and FocusRules fields for app/domain black/whitelist\n    status: pending\n  - id: onboarding-vpn\n    content: Document 5-step onboarding grant order including VpnService.prepare and verification checks\n    status: pending\n  - id: manifest-canonical\n    content: Document canonical manifest permission/service/queries list including BIND_VPN_SERVICE and FGS specialUse\n    status: pending\nisProject: false\n---\n# LifeOS Permissions Matrix (+ Network VPN Control) + Android Dev Environment\n\nSource of truth for features: [`.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md`](.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md). Stack remains **native Kotlin + Compose**.\n\nThis plan covers:\n\n1. **Cloud Agent environment** — Android SDK, **adb**, and build tooling so agents can compile, sideload, and inspect the app.\n2. **App permissions matrix** — every hackathon feature plus VpnService network blacklist/whitelist.\n\n---\n\n## Part A — Cloud Agent development environment (ADB + toolchain)\n\n### Locked choices\n\n- **Base image**: Cursor default Ubuntu image (JDK 21 is already present). Do not bake a custom Dockerfile unless the default image is missing a hard OS dependency after local install fails.\n- **SDK root**: `/opt/android-sdk` (world-readable; owned by `ubuntu`).\n- **Components installed once into the snapshot** (heavy, stable):\n  - Android **cmdline-tools** (latest)\n  - **platform-tools** → provides `adb`, `fastboot`\n  - **build-tools;34.0.0** (pin; bump only if AGP requires newer)\n  - **platforms;android-34** (compileSdk 34; align with project when scaffolded)\n  - **ndk** not required for this prototype — skip\n  - **emulator** + system image — **skip by default** (Cloud Agent VMs usually lack nested KVM; adb still works against a USB/network device or a user-attached emulator). Document `adb connect <host:port>` for remote devices.\n- **Build system**: project Gradle Wrapper (no global Gradle install required). `install` may download the wrapper jar/distribution on first use once the Android project exists.\n- **Secrets**: `GEMINI_API_KEY` (optional for offline demo fallback; required for live LLM). Do not put keys in `environment.json`.\n\n### environment.json shape (to propose after validation)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"LifeOS Android\",\n  \"install\": \"bash scripts/cloud-agent-install.sh\",\n  \"start\": \"bash scripts/cloud-agent-start.sh\"\n}\n```\n\nNo long-running `terminals` required until a project scaffold exists (no Metro/dev server). After the Android module exists, optional terminal: `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` is a one-shot build, not a terminal daemon.\n\n### `scripts/cloud-agent-install.sh` (idempotent)\n\n1. Ensure `JAVA_HOME` points at the system JDK 21.\n2. If `/opt/android-sdk/cmdline-tools/latest` missing → download Google cmdline-tools zip, unpack under `/opt/android-sdk/cmdline-tools/latest`.\n3. Export `ANDROID_HOME=/opt/android-sdk`, `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=$ANDROID_HOME`, prepend `$ANDROID_HOME/cmdline-tools/latest/bin`, `$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools`, `$ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/34.0.0` to `PATH` via a file under `/etc/profile.d/android-sdk.sh` **or** a repo-local `env.sh` sourced by the install/start scripts (prefer repo-local + explicit exports in scripts so snapshot/agents do not rely on login shells).\n4. `yes | sdkmanager --licenses` (non-interactive).\n5. `sdkmanager \"platform-tools\" \"platforms;android-34\" \"build-tools;34.0.0\"` — safe to re-run (idempotent).\n6. Smoke: `adb version`, `sdkmanager --version`, `javac -version`.\n7. If `android/` (or app module) exists: `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` (or `./gradlew tasks`) to warm caches; skip gracefully if the project is not scaffolded yet.\n\n### `scripts/cloud-agent-start.sh` (per boot)\n\n1. Re-export `ANDROID_HOME` / `PATH` (in case profile was not loaded).\n2. Start `adb` server: `adb start-server`.\n3. Print `adb devices -l` (empty device list is OK; proves adb works).\n4. Exit 0.\n\n### Validation evidence (before snapshot / propose)\n\n| Check | Pass criteria |\n| --- | --- |\n| `javac -version` | 21.x |\n| `adb version` | Android Debug Bridge version printed |\n| `sdkmanager --list_installed` | platform-tools, platforms;android-34, build-tools;34.0.0 present |\n| Install idempotence | Second `install` run exits 0 with no destructive re-download failure |\n| `adb start-server` + `adb devices` | Server starts; command succeeds (device may be empty) |\n\n### Env workflow after local green\n\nFollow create-environment skill: working VM → snapshot → `trigger-environment-build` with `environmentJson` (snapshot + install/start) → fresh cloud subagent verify → `propose-environment-json` with `buildId` → user Saves.\n\n---\n\n## Part B — App permissions matrix (+ VPN network control)\n\n### Design decisions (locked)\n\n- **App UI blocking** stays on `UsageStatsManager` + `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` (no AccessibilityService).\n- **Network restriction** uses a local **`VpnService`**: LifeOS becomes the device VPN endpoint and decides which apps/domains may leave the device. No root. No `WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS`.\n- Two complementary enforcement layers:\n  - **UI layer**: stop opening Instagram (overlay).\n  - **Network layer**: starve blacklisted destinations / non-whitelisted apps of connectivity.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Chat[Chat ActionExecutor] --> FocusRules[FocusRules]\n  FocusRules --> UIBlock[FocusService overlay]\n  FocusRules --> NetBlock[LifeOsVpnService]\n  UIBlock --> UsageStats[UsageStatsManager]\n  UIBlock --> Overlay[SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW]\n  NetBlock --> VpnConsent[VpnService.prepare]\n  NetBlock --> AppFilter[addAllowed or addDisallowedApplication]\n  NetBlock --> DnsFilter[Local DNS blacklist whitelist]\n```\n\n### Feature → permission matrix (hackathon in-scope)\n\n| Feature | What it needs from the OS | Permissions / APIs | Grant path | Play / policy note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Chat + Gemini | Outbound HTTPS | `INTERNET` | Install-time | None |\n| Persist goals/tasks/XP/memory | Local storage | None beyond normal app storage | N/A | None |\n| Dashboard / risk % / streak | Read own DataStore | None | N/A | None |\n| Personality + TTS wake line | `TextToSpeech` | None | N/A | None |\n| Notifications (focus ongoing, alarm fallback, VPN status) | Post notifications | `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` | Runtime dialog (API 33+) | None |\n| Exact alarms / demo wake-up | `AlarmManager.setAlarmClock` | `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM` | Settings: `ACTION_REQUEST_SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM`; gate with `canScheduleExactAlarms()` | Do **not** use `USE_EXACT_ALARM` (clock-app only) |\n| Full-screen alarm Activity | Launch over lock screen | `USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT` | Install-time; on API 34+ may need Settings if not auto-granted — fallback to high-priority notification via `canUseFullScreenIntent()` | Prefer alarm-style FSI use |\n| Survive reboot (restore alarms + focus/VPN intent) | Boot broadcast | `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED` | Install-time | None |\n| Keep CPU awake briefly while scheduling / overlay | Partial wake | `WAKE_LOCK` | Install-time | None |\n| Alarm / block haptic | Vibrator | `VIBRATE` | Install-time | None |\n| Detect foreground app (Instagram/Chrome) | Usage access | `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS` | Settings: `ACTION_USAGE_ACCESS_SETTINGS`; verify via `AppOpsManager` | Low scrutiny vs Accessibility |\n| Focus block overlay | Draw over other apps | `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | Settings: `ACTION_MANAGE_OVERLAY_PERMISSION`; verify `Settings.canDrawOverlays()` | Also helps background activity launch |\n| Focus session process | Long-running monitor | `FOREGROUND_SERVICE`, `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE` + manifest `specialUse` property | Install-time; ongoing notification required | Declare special-use justification in Play form at release |\n| App picker for blocklist | Resolve launcher apps | Manifest `<queries>` for `MAIN`/`LAUNCHER` | N/A | Prefer this over `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES` |\n| **Network blacklist / whitelist** | Local VPN routing | `BIND_VPN_SERVICE` on service; `INTERNET`; FGS types below; user VPN consent | System VPN consent via `VpnService.prepare()`; optional Always-on VPN is user Settings | Play VPN declaration at release; disclose that traffic is filtered on-device |\n\n### Network restriction — concrete behavior\n\nImplement `LifeOsVpnService : VpnService` with:\n\n1. **App-level routing** (fast path): `VpnService.Builder.addDisallowedApplication(pkg)` (blacklist) or `addAllowedApplication(pkg)` (whitelist). Whitelist mode always includes LifeOS plus an internal `SYSTEM_CRITICAL_ALLOW` set.\n2. **Domain-level filter**: TUN + local DNS stub; NXDOMAIN/sinkhole for blacklist hosts; whitelist-network mode only resolves allowlisted hosts. On-device only (no remote VPN server).\n3. **LLM actions**: `network_block_apps`, `network_allow_apps`, `network_block_domains`, `network_allow_domains`, `network_mode` (`off` | `blacklist` | `whitelist`).\n4. **Demo pairing**: UI-block Instagram **and** VPN-disallow its network (optionally blacklist `instagram.com` / `youtube.com` for Chrome).\n\nVPN manifest extras: `BIND_VPN_SERVICE` on service, intent filter `android.net.VpnService`, FGS `specialUse`, ongoing notification. Do not request `CONTROL_VPN` or location.\n\n### Onboarding grants (ordered)\n\n1. Notifications → `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`\n2. Exact alarms → `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM`\n3. Usage access → `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS`\n4. Display over other apps → `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW`\n5. Network control (VPN) → `VpnService.prepare()`\n\nVerify before Focus / Network toggles: `canScheduleExactAlarms()`, usage AppOps, `canDrawOverlays()`, `VpnService.prepare() == null`.\n\n### Manifest declare list (canonical)\n\n**Normal:** `INTERNET`, `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`, `VIBRATE`, `WAKE_LOCK`, `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED`, `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM`, `USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT`, `FOREGROUND_SERVICE`, `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE`\n\n**Special access:** `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS`, `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW`\n\n**Service-locked:** `BIND_VPN_SERVICE` (on `LifeOsVpnService` only)\n\n**Not a permission:** `<queries>` launcher intent, TTS, DataStore\n\n### Explicitly out of the declare list\n\n| Tempting API | Why avoided |\n| --- | --- |\n| `AccessibilityService` | Play declaration + Advanced Protection revocation |\n| `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES` | `<queries>` is enough |\n| `USE_EXACT_ALARM` | Clock-app only |\n| `READ_SMS` / `READ_CALL_LOG` | Default-handler only |\n| `REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS` | Declaration friction |\n| Background location | Irrelevant; high scrutiny |\n| Device Admin / MDM / root iptables | Not shippable for consumer focus app |\n\n### Vision-doc later (not hackathon)\n\n| Vision item | Permission / mechanism |\n| --- | --- |\n| Calendar sync | `READ_CALENDAR`, `WRITE_CALENDAR` |\n| Notification scraping | `NotificationListenerService` |\n| Health | Health Connect + `ACTIVITY_RECOGNITION` |\n| Voice input | `RECORD_AUDIO` |\n| Gmail API | OAuth `gmail.readonly` (CASA for prod) |\n| Moodle/Piazza | Account/API — no phone permission |\n\n### Hard walls\n\n- VPN cannot silently start without `prepare()` / Always-on user action.\n- VPN does not replace UI overlay blocking.\n- Missing packages on `addAllowed`/`addDisallowed` must be handled.\n- OEM battery killers can still stop FGS/VPN.\n- Android-only remains correct vs iOS entitlements.\n\n---\n\n## Deliverable after approval (execution order)\n\n1. **Environment first**: install Android SDK + platform-tools on this VM, write `scripts/cloud-agent-install.sh` / `start.sh`, prove `adb`/`sdkmanager`, snapshot → draft build → propose for Save.\n2. **Permissions docs**: update [`.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md`](.cursor/plans/lifeos_hackathon_prototype_7372d322.plan.md) or sibling `.cursor/plans/` file with Part B matrix, network actions, and onboarding VPN grant.\n3. Do **not** scaffold the full Android app unless separately requested — environment + permissions documentation are the scope of this plan.\n"}
````

